
$VER: DeepSpace User Docs Version 1.95 - Paragon
Instructions for playing Deep Space
 --------------------------------------------------

Deep Space is a Space Role Playing Game.  
The objective of the game is to make money and build your
empire to be the strongest in the galaxy.  One way to build your empire is 
to find a dead-ended sector (only one way into the sector), then create and 
fortify planets.  The more you fortify, the less the chances are that your 
empire can be crushed by other players in the game.  The fastest way to 
build a strong empire is to start a corporation and get other players to
join.  This way you can all work together at building the corporation's 
empire.  

To build a great empire takes lots of cash.  There are rumors running around
the galaxy that you can find contraband now and then. Hmmm, but where could 
one go and diker over prices to sell such stuff?  Another rumor I've heard
is that some of the Aliens have an enourmous amounts of wealth on their 
planet. But beware, some of them are also heavly fortified...

Then if you are REAL powerfull!?

+-----------+
| MAIN MENU |
+-----------+

 The Main Menu is available anytime during normal ship movement.  To bring
 up the Main Menu, simply press the [?] key.  Let's cover the commands 
 available for this menu.

 [A] ATTACK - This option will only work if there is another ship in your
     current sector.  If there are multiple ships, you will be asked 
     which player you wish to attack.  You can attack by DeepSpace 
     (sector #1) butonly if the other player has a negative morality.  
     If you do attack a good moral player, you could end up in jail.
     The attack is based on your ships offensive ability & the opponites
     defensive ability. Be carefull attacking Aliens! They might fight
     back at a later time! Make sure you can kill them. 

 [B] Enter Black Hole - A black hole can be either in a stable or in a un-
     stable condition.  If it is in a stable condition, you can enter
     the black hole and travel to the other end of the hole and back again
     without any problems.  Beware entering an un-stable black hole!  
     You could get your ship destroyed! The better the ship is in 
     defense, the more chances of making it through.
     
 [C] Communications - Takes you to the Communications Menu.

 [D] Data Base - Takes you to the Database Menu.

 [F] Fortify Sector - If you have Sector Protectors you can place
     them in a sector using this command.  You can either set them
     to offensive or defensive tactics.  If you set them to Offensive, 
     they will immediately explode when an Explorers ship enters the sector 
     on.  Set to Defensive the Explorer is given the chance to leave before 
     they explode.  These can not be placed in or by sector 1. If a
     corp member fortifies the same sector ALL of the protectors will
     be set as they selected (offense/defense).
 
 [H] Handle mines - This will allow you to drop or pickup mines in space.  
     These are smart mines and won't blow up you go into the sector.
     You also can not drop them by or near sector 1.
 
 [I] Information - Takes you to the Information Menu.

 [L] Look at Borders - If you have a scanner on your ship this will allow 
     you to scan your bordering sectors for Aliens, Players and etc..

 [M] Move - This will just prompt you to enter a sector you wish to
     travel to.  It will store this number in a buffer, for easy re-call,
     in case you have stopped before you got to your destination.  You can
     also enter the sector number with out using [M]ove command, but it 
     will not remember your sector number.
     
 [O] Orbit Planet - If a planet is in the sector where you are located,
     this option will allow you to choose to land on, or bomb the planet. 
     To bomb the planet you will have to have Explosives that can be
     purchased at DeepSpace port in sector 1.    
 
 [P] Port - If a trading port is located in the sector where you are 
     located, this will allow you to buy or sell Isotrophic crystal, 
     Replicators, & Cerium metals.  If you do this while traveling
     between ports you can make a profit.  If you are in sector 1 this 
     command will allow you to port at DeepSpace. At the DeepSpace
     port you can purchase many things, get information, visit people
     in jail (possibly break them out) ect...     
     
 [R] Corporation Menu - Takes you to the Corporation Menu    
     
 [T] Launch Torpedo - If your ship is capable to carry Torpedoes &
     you have purchased one at the DeepSpace port in sector 1, use
     this command to launch one in an adjacent sector.  They will 
     cause havoc in that sector for approximately 15 seconds.
 
 [Q] QUIT GAME - Duhhh.

+---------------------+
| COMMUNICATIONS MENU |
+---------------------+

 [E] Send private Space Mail - If you wish to send a note to another
     player with out anyone else reading it?  Use this option.
     
 [M] Message Base - This is where you can read/write messages that all
     other players in the game will be able to read.
      
 [R] Read private Space Mail - If you did not delete your private mail
     when logging on you can go re-read them using this option.
     
 [Q] Main Menu - Will return you to the game.

+----------------+
| DATA BASE MENU |
+----------------+

 [A] Use Port Automaton - A port automation will create a port in the 
     sector you placed it. There can not be another port in the same 
     sector. There is a limit to how many ports are allowed in the game 
     also. If you can not make one due to the limit being maxed out, you 
     will have to blow one up using explosives first before creating your
     own..
   
 [C] Clear/Add avoided sectors - This helps you remember what sector
     you do not want to go to. If you get blown up in a certain sector
     it will be automatically added to the list. You can also clear
     all sectors in the list.
     
 [D] Dump Cargo Bays - If you wish to empty your bays you can just be a
     "space litter bug".
     
 [G] Use Genesis - You have to buy these at the DeepSpace Port in sector 1. 
     Find a good sector to create your planet. Planets are very vulnerable 
     until you build up defenses around it and/or on it, but they can be worth 
     it in the long run. There are several stages of development which add
     advantageous capabilities. Can you say, "teleport me to another planet".
     
 [K] Show known sectors - Your ships computer will display all of the
     sectors you have previously visited.
      
 [L] List Aliens - You can see a list of all Aliens showing their statistics.
 
 [M] Rank Players by Morality - See who is bad or good.            
        
 [P] Launch Probe - You can select a destination sector for the probe
     to go to. It will show you what is in each sector along the way.
     It can also be easily destroyed by objects in a sector.
     
 [U] Show unknown sectors - Your ships computer will display all the
     sectors you have not been to.
     
 [V] Show avoided sectors - Will display all sectors in your avoid list.
 
 [Z] Course Plotter - The computer can show you what route it would
     take from one sector to another.
     
 [Q] Go back to the game.                
 
+------------------+
| INFORMATION MENU |
+------------------+
  
 [A] Toggle ANSI - This will toggle your display mode. You will be
     able to select between, ASCII, ANSI, IBM ANSI, & RIP.
     If RIP is selected you must be using a Terminal that supports
     RIP. No special icons are required. The Sysop can turn RIP
     off from the sysop menu, however the BBS does not have to
     support RIP Gfx for the remote user to use.
 
 [L] List Planets - Will list all planets that belong to you and your 
     Corporation (if you belong to one).
     
 [M] Show deployed Mines - Will list all mines you have placed in space 
     that you own. (and Corporation if applicable)
     
 [P] Show deployed Protectors - Will list all Sector Protectors in
     space that you own. (and Corporation if applicable)        

 [S] Stats - Will show your game statistics.
 
 [Q] Go back to the game.
